Generate a deterministic static completion definition for one explicitly supported shell.

Usage:
  cueson [global options] completion bash|zsh|fish|powershell

Options:
  None.

Global options:
  -q, --quiet  Suppress informational and success diagnostics.
  --silent     Suppress every non-error diagnostic.
  --no-color   Disable diagnostic color.
  -h, --help   Show help.
  --           End option processing; following paths and operands remain literal.

Notes:
  SHELL is case-sensitive. The command prints a script and never modifies a shell profile.

Streams:
  stdout  One static completion script for the selected shell.
  stderr  Errors and error-associated short usage.

Exit codes:
  0  Command or explicit help completed successfully; warnings may be present.
  1  An accepted operation failed during processing, cancellation, or runtime I/O.
  2  Command syntax, an operand, an option, or a pre-execution requirement was invalid.

Examples:
  cueson completion bash
  cueson completion powershell
